[{:db/id 17592186124463 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a9a907de-0404-5ffb-8362-e9676298070b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a9a907de-0404-5ffb-8362-e9676298070b" :question/id #uuid "a9a907de-0404-5ffb-8362-e9676298070b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36139" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}\n$$\n\n- The limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{3}$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$\n- The limit evaluates to $-1$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2}$\n- The limit exists and is equal to $\\frac{1}{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+2\\cdot 0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement I is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=-{x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=-{x}^{2}}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+2(-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{-{x}^{2}}{-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+2y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b798538-abe6-5e7d-a0f2-143f5a975750"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b798538-abe6-5e7d-a0f2-143f5a975750" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b798538-abe6-5e7d-a0f2-143f5a975750" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e7aeae6b-4c5c-573f-8a2d-c1af8e88ebf8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d84526b-47f3-51fb-a168-2cba08c88949" "answer-041632fd-d218-5815-9c69-da107f5da160" "answer-e7aeae6b-4c5c-573f-8a2d-c1af8e88ebf8" "answer-091e3fce-c81a-50bf-8d66-819204f1ee13" "answer-f5036257-dfe1-524a-b3ae-379280f91c23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d84526b-47f3-51fb-a168-2cba08c88949" :answer/id #uuid "4d84526b-47f3-51fb-a168-2cba08c88949" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-041632fd-d218-5815-9c69-da107f5da160" :answer/id #uuid "041632fd-d218-5815-9c69-da107f5da160" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7aeae6b-4c5c-573f-8a2d-c1af8e88ebf8" :answer/id #uuid "e7aeae6b-4c5c-573f-8a2d-c1af8e88ebf8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-091e3fce-c81a-50bf-8d66-819204f1ee13" :answer/id #uuid "091e3fce-c81a-50bf-8d66-819204f1ee13" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5036257-dfe1-524a-b3ae-379280f91c23" :answer/id #uuid "f5036257-dfe1-524a-b3ae-379280f91c23" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124564 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d70f2b2e-153e-52a8-b763-677074637b88" "question-fac05de1-cec1-5741-a5ec-beb8567ada24"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d70f2b2e-153e-52a8-b763-677074637b88" :question/id #uuid "d70f2b2e-153e-52a8-b763-677074637b88" :question/math-academy-id "q-74955" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{xy+2}-2}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4}=$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{xy+2}-2}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+2}-2}{{2}^{2}\\cdot {1}^{2}-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{xy+2}-2}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{xy+2}-2)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)}{({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{xy+2})^{2}-4}{({x}^{2}{y}^{2}-4)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{xy-2}{(xy-2)(xy+2)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{1}{(xy+2)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,1)}\\frac{1}{(xy+2)(\\sqrt{xy+2}+2)} & =\\frac{1}{(2\\cdot 1+2)(\\sqrt{2\\cdot 1+2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{16}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-356ed38c-7b44-5965-81ac-2c88dd16e0ea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-356ed38c-7b44-5965-81ac-2c88dd16e0ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "356ed38c-7b44-5965-81ac-2c88dd16e0ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4272af7f-33bd-5340-9cab-dc535b5219ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-af13b1b6-a010-5d4f-9f5a-9200139b2880" "answer-4272af7f-33bd-5340-9cab-dc535b5219ee" "answer-195220e5-a0bf-53a4-9715-d520b9cc06cf" "answer-6e9919cf-e851-589f-8631-eb084d75d2b4" "answer-1408b7a6-0c53-5b8e-9133-67f17a92be59"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af13b1b6-a010-5d4f-9f5a-9200139b2880" :answer/id #uuid "af13b1b6-a010-5d4f-9f5a-9200139b2880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4272af7f-33bd-5340-9cab-dc535b5219ee" :answer/id #uuid "4272af7f-33bd-5340-9cab-dc535b5219ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-195220e5-a0bf-53a4-9715-d520b9cc06cf" :answer/id #uuid "195220e5-a0bf-53a4-9715-d520b9cc06cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e9919cf-e851-589f-8631-eb084d75d2b4" :answer/id #uuid "6e9919cf-e851-589f-8631-eb084d75d2b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1408b7a6-0c53-5b8e-9133-67f17a92be59" :answer/id #uuid "1408b7a6-0c53-5b8e-9133-67f17a92be59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124459 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-113d22b7-0222-5499-8d44-de1af29900a0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-113d22b7-0222-5499-8d44-de1af29900a0" :question/id #uuid "113d22b7-0222-5499-8d44-de1af29900a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-129340" :question/problem "Determine ${lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{3}-xy}{{x}^{3}y}.$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{3}-xy}{{x}^{3}y} & =\\frac{{0}^{3}-2(0)}{{2}^{3}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{3}-xy}{{x}^{3}y} & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{y({y}^{2}-x)}{{x}^{3}y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{\\cancel{y}({y}^{2}-x)}{{x}^{3}\\cancel{y}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{{x}^{3}} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}-2}{{2}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-926f9639-4822-59a3-b1ce-00790077ea5e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-926f9639-4822-59a3-b1ce-00790077ea5e" :answer-field/id #uuid "926f9639-4822-59a3-b1ce-00790077ea5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-88efc86f-081f-55bf-ae7a-919620a60363" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ada75cf0-6667-5096-ac74-83cbe5d47353" "answer-88efc86f-081f-55bf-ae7a-919620a60363" "answer-ab3f8034-9dc3-50c6-bd5e-b2ea032262ec" "answer-638f4f88-2af6-5eb2-9ed5-e5ceca460c65" "answer-194293e4-0f48-56b7-8094-db759002b936"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ada75cf0-6667-5096-ac74-83cbe5d47353" :answer/id #uuid "ada75cf0-6667-5096-ac74-83cbe5d47353" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88efc86f-081f-55bf-ae7a-919620a60363" :answer/id #uuid "88efc86f-081f-55bf-ae7a-919620a60363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab3f8034-9dc3-50c6-bd5e-b2ea032262ec" :answer/id #uuid "ab3f8034-9dc3-50c6-bd5e-b2ea032262ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-638f4f88-2af6-5eb2-9ed5-e5ceca460c65" :answer/id #uuid "638f4f88-2af6-5eb2-9ed5-e5ceca460c65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-194293e4-0f48-56b7-8094-db759002b936" :answer/id #uuid "194293e4-0f48-56b7-8094-db759002b936" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fac05de1-cec1-5741-a5ec-beb8567ada24" :question/id #uuid "fac05de1-cec1-5741-a5ec-beb8567ada24" :question/math-academy-id "q-129343" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{y+z}{\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{y+z}{\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z}} & =\\frac{1+(-1)}{\\sqrt{2-1}-\\sqrt{2+(-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-1}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{y+z}{\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{(y+z)(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})}{(\\sqrt{x-y}-\\sqrt{x+z})(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{(y+z)(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})}{(x-y)-(x+z)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{(y+z)(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})}{-(y+z)} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}\\frac{\\cancel{(y+z)}(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})}{\\cancel{(y+z)}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{lim}_{x\\to (2,1,-1)}(\\sqrt{x-y}+\\sqrt{x+z}) & =-(\\sqrt{2-1}+\\sqrt{2+(-1)}) \\\\  & =-(1+1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e093674e-caf5-5f8d-97ff-ca3172fa6889"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e093674e-caf5-5f8d-97ff-ca3172fa6889" :answer-field/id #uuid "e093674e-caf5-5f8d-97ff-ca3172fa6889" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4005330f-5c8b-5294-9f96-5e9be2626147" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4005330f-5c8b-5294-9f96-5e9be2626147" "answer-39f90210-da8d-511b-9d38-b3d158c315d4" "answer-88b04b8f-a6d9-5b86-ba06-a0